(* EXPECT-ERROR: a string literal can be lent only to an RO parameter *)
(* A checked language that segfaults.  Observed 2026-10-01, in the
   released 0.13.0, while constant tables were being built: a
   by-value STR parameter can be written through, a string literal is
   read-only data, and nothing connected the two -- this program
   passed the checker and died with SIGSEGV at the assignment, exit
   139, no IndexError and no message.  The same through an RO
   parameter lent onward to a writable one.  Counted before the rule
   was chosen: three calls in four trees handed read-only storage to
   a by-value slice and none of the callees wrote, so nothing that
   ran had met it; the 164 procedures that DO write through a
   by-value slice were all given real arrays.  The rule is at the
   call (par 2.4): read-only storage goes only to an RO parameter. *)
MODULE m ;
PROCEDURE Up (s: STR) RAISES IndexError =
BEGIN
  s[0] := 'X'
END Up ;
PROCEDURE F () RAISES IndexError =
BEGIN
  Up ('abc')
END F ;
END m.
